{
  "name": "Unraid · Docker updates & actions",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Unraid · Docker updates & actions\n- **Weekly update window** (Sunday 04:00): refreshes image digests and updates every container with a new image, except **cfg.excludeFromUpdates**. Reports to Telegram only when something was updated or failed.\n- **From Telegram bot**: commands forwarded by the *Sysadmin & Telegram bot* workflow:\n  /containers · /updates · /update_all · /update_<name> · /restart_<name> · /start_<name> · /stop_<name> · /logs_<name>\n  /update_all and /stop_<name> ask for confirmation first (tap the _confirm command).\n\nContainer names in commands use underscores (Plex-Media-Server → /logs_plex_media_server).",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 360
      },
      "id": "a622bccd-a3e8-44b1-abc5-50a22370b4f7",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup\n1. Select the **Unraid API** and **Telegram** credentials.\n2. **Settings**: set **cfg.telegramChatId** (for the weekly report) and the containers to exclude from automatic updates. Keep **n8n** excluded: updating it recreates the container running this workflow, so the run is cut off. Update n8n by hand.\n3. Publish / activate: the schedule needs it, and the bot calls the published version.\n4. Copy this workflow's ID (from its URL) into the bot workflow's **Run Docker workflow** node.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b504b21f-feb9-4c3e-a0a1-2a3fff1231da",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -400
